; Stage 14 UN-2 negative fixture: `(ns unsafe)` is rejected.
;
; `unsafe` is a reserved pseudo-namespace (design/stage14/unsafe-namespace.md
; D1) — the `unsafe/<op>` heads are routed by special-form head-identity
; dispatch, not real namespace resolution, so no user code may ever declare a
; real namespace called `unsafe` (that would make `unsafe/whatever` ambiguous
; between "reserved op" and "someone's namespace member"). Compiling this must
; FAIL with:
;   "'unsafe' is a reserved namespace name"
(ns unsafe)

(defn noop ():i32
  (return 0))
